 {"version_id": "struct-09", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Add a structured hypothesis-test-revise loop that requires the agent to record the failing assertion, likely cause, smallest corrective edit, and rerun result after each substantive change.", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + \"\"\"\n\nUse an iterative validation loop", "replace": "TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + \"\"\"\n\nUse an iterative validation loop with explicit state: after every substantive edit, run the narrowest reproducer or focused test, capture the complete failure and traceback, write a one-sentence root-cause hypothesis, make the smallest corrective edit, and rerun the same check. Do not broaden to the full suite until the focused check passe"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.87, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.89, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.88, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.34}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.31}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.045, "why": "The explicit hypothesis-test-revise loop directly improves validation and iterative debugging, producing the largest execution-accuracy gain. It can still iterate on an initially incorrect repository model and may incur test-running overhead, so target alignment and complex-case gains remain below the strongest diagnosis-focused version."}
 {"version_id": "struct-10", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Strengthen patch selection with an evidence hierarchy that requires behavioral proof, regression coverage, and consistency with the issue contract before accepting a candidate.", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "target_alignment", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "# EVIDENCE GATE:\nReject patches that are merely plausible. Prefer candidates with focused test evid", "replace": "# EVIDENCE GATE:\nReject patches that are merely plausible. First verify that the candidate changes the implementation path identified by the issue, then require a focused reproducer or test demonstrating the requested behavior, relevant regression coverage, and consistency with existing public API and error semantics. Penalize broad unrelated edits, tests that do not exercise the changed path, and"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.9, "reasoning_soundness": 0.9, "execution_accuracy": 0.78, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.8675, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.29}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.26}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0325, "why": "The evidence gate discourages plausible but unverified patches and improves contract reasoning and patch selection. However, requiring behavioral proof and regression coverage can make the agent overly conservative when tests are difficult or unavailable, reducing execution accuracy and limiting gains on the hardest probes."}
 {"version_id": "struct-11", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Normalize candidate patch metadata at construction time and derive a reliable non-empty-diff indicator so empty or malformed candidate outputs cannot be treated as successful patches.", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "        self.cleaned_patch = cleaned_patch.strip() if isinstance(cleaned_patch, str) else self.patch", "replace": "        self.cleaned_patch = cleaned_patch.strip() if isinstance(cleaned_patch, str) else self.patch\n        self.has_patch_content = bool(self.cleaned_patch and self.cleaned_patch not in {\"diff --git\", \"---\", \"+++\"})"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.82, "execution_accuracy": 0.8, "output_integrity": 0.94}, "aggregate": 0.855, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.22}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.18}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.02, "why": "Reliable patch-content normalization prevents empty or malformed outputs from being treated as successful, giving a clear output-integrity improvement. It does not improve diagnosis, implementation, or validation of substantive repository changes, so probe resolution remains essentially at baseline."}
+{"version_id": "struct-12", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Make success metadata conservative by requiring both the reported success flag and actual cleaned patch content before exposing a candidate as a successful patch.", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "        self.is_success_patch = bool(is_success_patch)", "replace": "        self.is_success_patch = bool(is_success_patch and self.cleaned_patch and self.has_patch_content)"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.82, "execution_accuracy": 0.8, "output_integrity": 0.95}, "aggregate": 0.8575, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.22}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.18}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0225, "why": "Requiring both a success flag and actual patch content makes success reporting more conservative and improves output integrity slightly beyond normalization alone. It provides no substantive solving capability and can suppress a result if metadata is incomplete, so execution and probe scores stay at baseline."}
+{"version_id": "struct-13", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Reconnaissance-first execution contract", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + \"\"\"\n\nFor framework and scientific-library changes: build a behavior matrix before editing:", "replace": "TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + \"\"\"\n\nBefore editing, perform a reconnaissance phase: identify the issue's likely entry points, trace callers and callees, inspect related tests and alternate implementations, and record the smallest set of files that can explain the behavior. Do not patch until you can state the current control flow, the intended control flow, and why the chose"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.89, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.82, "output_integrity": 0.87}, "aggregate": 0.8625, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.3}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.25}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0275, "why": "Reconnaissance directly addresses repository-specific diagnosis and should improve path tracing on the difficult Django and Astropy tasks. The incomplete-looking instruction and added pre-edit overhead limit execution gains."}
diff --git a/trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py b/trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py
index b44e12d..c9e0679 100644
--- a/trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py
+++ b/trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ For framework and scientific-library changes, build a behavior matrix before edi
 
 TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + """
 
+Use an iterative validation loop with explicit state: maintain a compact ledger containing the current hypothesis, supporting evidence, contradicting evidence, exact reproducer, latest edit, and next experiment. After each failure, update the ledger before editing again; do not repeat an unchanged hypothesis or test command unless the environment changed.
+
 Use an iterative validation loop with explicit state: after every substantive edit, run the narrowest reproducer or focused test, capture the complete failure and traceback, write a one-sentence root-cause hypothesis, make the smallest corrective edit, and rerun the same check. Do not broaden to the full suite until the focused check passes; after it passes, run relevant regression tests and inspect any new failures rather than stopping at the first green result. after every substantive edit: run the narrowest reproducer or focused test, inspect the complete failure, revise the patch, and rerun it. Before finishing, run relevant regression tests and continue debugging until the result is passing or a concrete environmental blocker is documented.
 """
 
